If you want to use the Jenkins Shared Library from a Jenkins Pipeline, use this setup.

1. Shared Library GitHub repo

Private repo:

jenkins-shared-library/
└── vars/
    └── hello.groovy

vars/hello.groovy:

def call() {
    echo "Hello from Jenkins Shared Library!"
}

2. Jenkinsfile in your application repo
@Library('Shared') _

pipeline {
    agent any

    stages {

        stage('Checkout') {
            steps {
                git(
                    branch: 'main',
                    credentialsId: 'github-private',
                    url: 'https://github.com/YOUR_USERNAME/YOUR_APP_REPO.git'
                )
            }
        }

        stage('Shared Library Test') {
            steps {
                hello()
            }
        }

        stage('Build') {
            steps {
                sh 'echo "Building application..."'
            }
        }
    }
}

Replace:

YOUR_USERNAME
YOUR_APP_REPO
3. Important: Configure Shared

In Jenkins:

Manage Jenkins → System → Global Pipeline Libraries → Add

Set:

Name: Shared
Default version: main

Then configure your private GitHub repository:

Repository:
https://github.com/YOUR_USERNAME/jenkins-shared-library.git

Select your GitHub credential:

github-private

Save.

4. Your pipeline syntax

The first line must be exactly:

@Library('Shared') _

The _ is required when loading the library globally.

If you want to load the library directly from Pipeline

You can also use:

@Library('Shared@main') _

pipeline {
    agent any

    stages {
        stage('Test') {
            steps {
                hello()
            }
        }
    }
}

This tells Jenkins to use the main version of your Shared library.
